*.tmp

# What is measured on the bench stays on the bench.  `data/` holds the three kinds
# of bench artifact: `data/captures/` the two Windows serial-monitor sessions the
# vendor app was watched through (39 MB of text, plus the `.spm` binaries only the
# monitoring tool can open), `data/glass/` the log of every window run made against
# the real panel, `data/vendor_frames/` the 65 `.osd` payloads lifted out of the
# captures by `tools/vendor_capture.py --extract`.  None of it is published: the
# captures and the logs both carry this panel's own serial number, and editing a
# log to take it out would be tampering with the evidence rather than redacting it.
#
# The consequence is stated where it matters rather than here: every wall-clock,
# byte-count and pixel figure in README.md and PROTOCOL.md traces to a file in this
# directory on the author's machine, and the file names are quoted so a run can be
# repeated, not so it can be read here.  The checks that would read them -
# `tools/verify_protocol.py`, `tools/theme_check.py --arc`, and the two selftest
# sections that call them - say out loud that they are skipping instead of passing.
data/

# python packaging and editors
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store

# debhelper's working state, and the binary package trees it assembles from
# debian/tmp before dpkg-deb packs them.  The .deb/.changes/.buildinfo themselves
# are written one directory up, outside the tree, by dpkg-buildpackage.  Listed by
# name rather than by `debian/*/` because debian/source/ and debian/tests/ are
# source files like the rest of debian/.
.pybuild/
debhelper-build-stamp
debian/tmp/
debian/.debhelper/
debian/debhelper-build-stamp
debian/files
debian/*.substvars
debian/*.debhelper.log
debian/*.debhelper
debian/xigmatek-connect-lcd/
debian/xigmatek-connect-lcd-themes/
